<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Balkan League</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1912–1913</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Balkan League was the alliance formed in 1912 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> and Montenegro against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>, built on a series of bilateral treaties. Its members defeated the Ottomans in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-balkan-war">First Balkan War</a> of 1912–1913, driving them from most of their European lands. The league broke apart over the division of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonia-region">Macedonia</a>, which led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-balkan-war">Second Balkan War</a> in 1913.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/balkan-league.jpg" alt="Balkan League" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sp. Markezinis · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Balkans_at_1913.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
